If \(R_{n}(z)\) is the remainder after \(n\) terms then

**7.1.24**: \[R_{n}(z)=(-1)^{n}\,\frac{1\cdot 3\ldots\,(2n-1)}{(2z^{2})^{n}}\;\theta,\] \[\theta=\!\int_{0}^{\infty}\!e^{-t}\left(1\!+\!\frac{t}{z^{2}}\right) ^{-n-1}dt\qquad\left(|\arg\,z|\!<\!\frac{\pi}{2}\right)\] \[|\theta|\!<\!1\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\left(|\arg\,z|\!<\!\frac{ \pi}{4}\right)\]

For \(x\) real, \(R_{n}(x)\) is less in absolute value than the first neglected term and of the same sign.

